+## Conversation list (#144)
+
+- `list_conversations` is statically valid with no payload, an optional integer `limit` from 1 through 200, and an optional composite `before: {updatedAt, sessionId}` cursor whose timestamp is a parseable ISO string; invalid limits or incomplete or invalid cursors are rejected with an error naming the field ([validated by: validates history limits and complete ISO cursors independently of opt-in](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L113)).
+- With `transport.history.enabled`, a request receives exactly one `conversation_list` with newest-first summaries containing only `sessionId`, ISO-string `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, and `entryCount`; the authenticated connection supplies the user id even if the frame supplies another, `{limit, before}` reaches `listFor` unchanged, responses are never pushed or terminated with `stream_end`, and a listed id opens through the existing ownership-checked resume and replay path ([validated by: lists only the authenticated owner, pages ties without loss, and reopens a listed conversation](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L131)).
+- History defaults off independently of resume, explicit disablement stays off, and a store without `listFor` cannot list; each case answers exactly one `UNSUPPORTED` error instead of an empty history and keeps the connection open ([validated by: answers disabled history and a store without listFor with UNSUPPORTED rather than an empty history](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L168)).
+- A history request is answered outside the turn lock, before `stream_end` even while a turn on the same session is waiting in its model lifecycle hook ([validated by: answers history while a real turn is held in its lifecycle hook, before stream_end](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L184)).
+- A failing history store answers one sanitized `SERVER_ERROR`, logs the session id without user content and leaves the socket open; a store unable to list because its collection has no `find` answers `UNSUPPORTED` instead ([validated by: sanitizes a real disconnected database failure and distinguishes a collection without find](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L231)).
+
+The list discloses only one authenticated user’s conversation metadata, without conversation content. The user id comes from the connection, never the frame; `transport.history` is the deployer’s separate decision to make that personal history reachable from the client. Retention remains the consumer’s responsibility under re-cinq/HALEngine#41.
